The two pop stars revealed Tuesday (Oct. 13) that the Midwest Princess will be jumping on a revamped version of &#8220;Expectations&#8221; from Rodrigo&#8217;s Billboard 200 -topping third studio album, you seem pretty sad for a girl so in love. Both the song and an accompanying visual will drop Thursday (Oct. 15), two days after the &#8220;Drop Dead&#8221; singer teased the team-up by sharing an audio snippet of Roan&#8217;s voice saying, &#8220;Oh, Olivia does remixes now.&#8221;

Writing that she was &#8220;beyond excited&#8221; to share the news, Rodrigo also unveiled the &#8220;Expectations&#8221; remix&#8217;s cover art shot by Phoenix Johnson, showing the two pop stars posing on top of a retro convertible in Cyndi Lauper-esque 1980s outfits.

&#8220;Expectations&#8221; arrived alongside Rodrigo&#8217;s most recent LP in June, debuting at No. 20 on the Billboard Hot 100 . The two women have been friends for a long time, having both worked with producer Dan Nigro for years. In August, the &#8220;Good Luck, Babe!&#8221; artist played a set at Rodrigo&#8217;s inaugural Daisy Chain Fields festival in Irvine, Calif., which raised $20 million for charities supporting women and girls.

In 2022, Roan opened a show on Rodrigo&#8217;s Sour Tour before serving as a supporting act on the Guts World Tour two years later. After Roan shot to global stardom later in 2024, she reunited with Rodrigo on the Guts trek to sing &#8220;Hot to Go!&#8221; in Los Angeles.

&#8220;She actually gives me so much advice on taking care of myself and being me in an industry that&#8217;s so overwhelming sometimes,&#8221; Rodrigo told Billboard of Roan in October 2024. &#8220;I really appreciate her.&#8221;

